---
description: Workout, exercise, combination, and rating domain invariants.
globs: src/{domain,features}/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

Read `docs/domain-model.md`, `docs/domain-glossary.md`, and `docs/feedback-system.md` before changing domain behavior.

- A workout contains ordered blocks; blocks contain ordered workout items.
- A workout item is an exercise or a standalone break.
- MVP exercise modes are `rounds` and `continuous`; `strength` is reserved for future implementation.
- One exercise contains one combination or one instruction.
- Preserve `combinationId` when available and always store an immutable exercise-name snapshot.
- Discipline becomes locked after the first exercise is added.
- Skipped exercises never receive rating zero and never enter averages.
- Unrated exercises never enter averages.
- Keep completion quantity separate from subjective execution quality.
- Exercise execution uses one 1–5 scale.
- Perceived workout progress uses a separate 1–7 scale.
- Goal-completion feedback is shown only when the workout has a main goal.
